  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any automatic market ban at 5% failure and makes sales restriction discretionary, which substantially favours Northwind's Hearth 10. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which would apply to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S4's 36-month suppression lead time matches Halcyon's stated position. S1 is strict for both companies, and S3's 72-month retrofit period sits within the acceptable range but gives Northwind more time for its 38% shut-off coverage."
